    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:ec46e3209ab74818",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "e0e9984a0a15fb70d7a2acb83761a9224e8005b781a5420819ac6a2e115deb05",
      "text": "After breakfast, transfer to the airport for your flight to Foz do Iguaçu, where you are welcomed and taken to your hotel. Then set off on a tour of the falls. On the border of Brazil, Argentina and Paraguay, within a national park of unique flora and fauna, 275 waterfalls, each with its own name, crash into the canyon of the Devil’s Throat; their name means “big water” in Guarani. The contrast between the calm, almost lazy river above the falls and the boiling torrents plunging into the gorge below is stunning: you could watch this spectacle for hours.\n\nOptional, at an additional cost: the Macuco Safari and the Bird Park (see Optional excursions).\n\nNot included: Flight Rio de Janeiro – Foz do Iguaçu",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "word_exact",
